    "narrative": "The spotlight today belongs to **Jose Caballero**, who paces the squad with a massive 80.26 efficiency score. While his slotting at #7 in the order historically tempers expectations, the intersection of a favorable matchup against Hudson and a significant boost from wind conditions makes him our primary weapon for chasing stolen bases and counting stats. **Tyler Soderstrom** also provides a high-floor start at 61.62, anchored by a positive park factor and a central spot in the order, while **Josh Naylor** remains a cornerstone at 1B with a 66.36 rating, benefiting from an advantageous platoon look against Baz.\n\nWhile we remain aggressive, we are exercising strict discipline regarding our bench threshold. **Travis Bazzana** serves as our most notable exclusion today; despite his lead-off role providing a +10 buffer to his profile, the combination of a tough matchup against Drohan and a significant platoon penalty dropped his efficiency to 37.03, falling safely below our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor.\" We are comfortable leaving **Travis Bazzana** on the pine to protect our game caps. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the status of **Trevor Story**, who remains sidelined on the IL, and we are managing the roster absences of **Corbin Carroll** and **James Wood**, both of whom are unavailable due to the team off-day. \n\nWe are tracking the remaining lineup volatility closely, specifically for **Cole Young** and **Brice Turang**. **Cole Young** sits at a marginal 46.76; while his speed gives him a slight edge against a slower delivery, he requires a clean run-scoring environment to justify the cap hit. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** faces a difficult task against the high-skill arm of Messick; his score of 49.95 keeps him just above the bench line, but he represents a high-risk asset in today\u2019s rotation. With no other major weather flags on the board, we are prioritizing the **Jose Caballero** and **Tyler Soderstrom** pairing to anchor our offensive output.",
